    "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.10.09.17.50.47/orleindustries.ipgkit.setup.1.0.0-rc.6.json#deprecation",
    "message": "Security: upgrade to 1.0.0-rc.7. In 1.0.0-rc.6 and earlier, the create-payment endpoint accepted a consumer id and a payment-link id from the request body, so one API consumer could create a payment attributed to another consumer (who then received a validly signed payment.created webhook) or attach it to another consumer's payment link. Fixed in 1.0.0-rc.7, which also brings breaking contract changes and three database migrations; see the upgrade guide.",
    "reasons": [
      "Other",
      "Legacy",
      "CriticalBugs"
    ]
  },
  "description": "IpgKit first-run setup wizard Razor Class Library: anonymous /Setup/* pages that bootstrap a fresh deployment (DB connection, admin creds, JWT/HMAC keys, adapter choice, branding) without editing appsettings or shelling onto the server. Consume via AddIpgKitSetup / UseIpgKitSetup. Runtime no-op when SetupState.Status = Completed or when IpgKit:Setup:Mode = Headless.",
